    "Lunar years 1900-2099, one integer per year (index 0 = 1900): Ho Ngoc Duc's precomputed tables (UTC+7), as shipped in @dqcai/vn-lunar 1.0.1 (MIT) as TK20 and TK21.",
    "Decoding a year y with value v:",
    "  tetOffset  = v >> 17          days from 1 January of y (solar) to lunar 1/1 of y",
    "  leapLength = 29 + ((v >> 16) & 1)",
    "  monthBits  = (v >> 4) & 0xFFF   bit 11 = month 1 ... bit 0 = month 12; 1 = 30 days, 0 = 29 days",
    "  leapMonth  = v & 0xF          0 = no leap month; otherwise the leap month follows that month",
    "Months run 1..leapMonth, leap month, leapMonth+1..12, each starting where the previous ends."
